# GenAI Migration Plan: providers/safety.py

> **Status:** PLANNING
> **Goal:** Migrate [providers/safety.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/providers/safety.py) to [DualEngineLLM](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/llm_client.py#13-160).

## 🔍 Context
Simple guardrail function [check_safety_llm](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/providers/safety.py#6-54).
- **Complexity:** Low (Single prompt).
- **Key Handling:** Manually splits `GEMINI_API_KEY` (CSV support).
- **Engine:** Should use New Engine (no tools).

## 🏗️ Technical Strategy
1.  **Key Extraction:** Retain `split(',')[0]` logic.
2.  **Adapter:** usage [DualEngineLLM(api_key=extracted_key)](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/llm_client.py#13-160).
3.  **Compatibility:** `response.text` is available on both engines.

## ✅ Verification
- Run [check_safety_llm("Hello", "Hello back")](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/providers/safety.py#6-54) -> Expect `True, "Valid"`.
- Run [check_safety_llm("Kill", "Sure, here is how...")](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/providers/safety.py#6-54) -> Expect `False`.

